 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the city of Amsterdam, in the county of Montgomery, to\nfinance a certain deficit by the issuance of bonds",
    "basePrintNo": "S6465",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6465-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Montgomery County",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6465\n\nSPONSOR: AMEDORE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to authorize the city of Amsterdam, in the\ncounty of Montgomery, to finance a certain deficit by the issuance of\nbonds\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to allow the City of Amsterdam to finance a\ncertain deficit by the issuance of bonds.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the City of Amsterdam to issue $8.3 million in\nbonds to liquidate the cumulative deficits in the general fund, trans-\nportation fund, sewer fund, and recreation fund accumulated during\nfiscal years ended June 30, 2008 through 2018, inclusive.\n\nSection 2 requires that the State Comptroller determine the deficit\nbefore the issuance of bonds. This section also directs the City of\nAmsterdam to submit a report detailing the amount and cause of the defi-\ncit, the City's independent audit report and other information the Comp-\ntroller may find necessary.\n\nSection 3 makes the probable useful life of the bonds ten years,\ncomputed from the date of such bonds or from the date of the first bond\nanticipation note issued in anticipation of the sale of such bonds,\nwhichever date is earlier.\n\nSection 4 makes the sale and issuance of deficit financing bonds subject\nto the State Local Finance Law and indicates that these bonds will not\nbe subject to either mandatory or permissive referendum.\n\nSection 5(a) requires the preparation by the City Mayor of quarterly\nreports of expenditure and revenues that must be submitted to each\nmember of the City Council, the Director of the NYS Division of the\nBudget, the State Comptroller, and the Chairs of the Senate Finance\nCommittee and the Assembly Ways and Means Committee.\n\n(b) For each fiscal year occurring during the time of which bonds and/or\nbond anticipation notes issued pursuant to this act are outstanding, the\nMayor of the City of Amsterdam shall also prepare a quarterly trial\nbalance of general and special fund ledger accounts.\n\n(c) Beginning July 1, 2019 and for each fiscal year thereafter during\nwhich said debt remains outstanding, the City Mayor or officer responsi-\nble for the preparation of the tentative budget shall submit the tenta-\ntive budget for the next succeeding fiscal year to the State Comptroller\nno later than thirty days before the last date on which the budget must\nbe finally adopted.\n\n(d) Within 90 days of the issuance of any debt pursuant to this act and\nfor each fiscal year thereafter during which said debt remains outstand-\ning, the Mayor of the City of Amsterdam or officer in charge of drafting\nbudget, within 30 days after the final adoption of the budget for the\nnext succeeding fiscal year, shall prepare a 3-year financial plan\ncovering the next succeeding fiscal year and the 2 fiscal years there-\nafter that includes all provisions that are required by subdivision 10\nof section 54 of the State Finance law.  Copies of the plan should be\nsent to the Mayor and Chief Fiscal Officer of the City of Amsterdam, the\nNYS Director of the Division of the Budget, the State Comptroller, the\nChairs of the Assembly Ways and Means Committee and the Senate Finance\nCommittee.\n\n(e) For each fiscal year during which said debt remains outstanding, the\nchief fiscal officer of the city of Amsterdam shall notify the State\nComptroller at least 15 days prior to the issuance of any bonds or notes\nand the State Comptroller may review and make recommendations regarding\nthe affordability to the city of Amsterdam of any such proposed issuance\nor contract, provided, however, that the validity of any bond antic-\nipation note or bond issued to refinance a maturing bond anticipation\nnote shall not be affected by any failure to provide such notice in a\ntimely manner.\n\nSection 6 and 7 authorize the sale of the deficit financing bonds and\nstate that judgments against one section of this act will not invalidate\nthe other sections\n\nSection 8 provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe City of Amsterdam has requested this special legislation. Current\nState law does not allow the City of Amsterdam to liquidate its deficit.\nThis type of financing has traditionally been authorized by the Legisla-\nture for individual municipalities. The oversight provisions included in\nthis bill will enable the City of Amsterdam to avoid future fiscal and\nbudgetary problems.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
